        "original_id": "81dfdbac-1083-5a5a-b298-4deee240750c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paola Suárez, Virginia Ruano Pascual, Michael Venus, Chan Hao-ching, Monica Niculescu, Max Mirnyi, Ashleigh Barty, John Peers\n- Topics: Tennis doubles, Grand Slam titles, rankings, 2014 US Open mixed doubles\n\nFacts:\n- Paola Suárez, born on 23 June 1976, is a retired professional tennis player from Argentina.\n- Paola Suárez was one of the most prominent women's doubles players in the early and mid-2000s.\n- Paola Suárez won eight Grand Slam titles in women's doubles, and all eight were with Virginia Ruano Pascual.\n- Paola Suárez held the world No. 1 doubles ranking for 87 non-consecutive weeks.\n- Michael Venus reached a career-high singles ranking of No. 274 in July 2011.\n- Michael Venus became better known as a leading doubles player with a huge serve.\n- At the 2014 US Open mixed doubles event, Max Mirnyi partnered with Chan Hao-ching and lost in the second round to Ashleigh Barty and John Peers.\n- In 2017, Chan Hao-ching reached the Wimbledon women's doubles final with Monica Niculescu.\n- In 2017, Chan Hao-ching also reached the US Open mixed doubles final with Michael Venus.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
